rong class='sig'>+0.31\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.18 to +0.44), about +2.3\u00b0F since 1952. Binghamton's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.30\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.16 to +0.45), about +2.2\u00b0F since 1952.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Binghamton has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Binghamton's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+1.50 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.85 to +2.15), about +10.9 inches since 1952. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 42.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (68.05 in); the driest, 1981 (30.26 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}